  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Entry points",
      "items": [
        "VS Code extension: finds package-lock.json, validates locally, modal consent names the API URL, then polls scan status and findings",
        "Dashboard: upload or GitHub-repo scans; on Vercel /api/* and /health are rewritten to the Render API so the session cookie stays first-party",
        "GitHub Action: reads the base lockfile from the PR base SHA, runs app.gate, posts/updates one PR comment and fails on verdict 'fail'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Scan pipeline (services.py analyze_scan)",
      "items": [
        "parse_lockfile v1-v3 -> build_dependency_graph (NetworkX, nearest-ancestor resolution)",
        "npm metadata fetch_many (cache, semaphore, retries) -> OSV known-vulnerability check on every release",
        "Baseline = latest complete scan of the same project and owner; change rules: new-dependency, dependency-expansion, publisher-change, install-script, provenance-removed, unusual-release-timing",
        "Optional Gemini rerank; AiRankingError keeps deterministic order. Failure stores only the exception type",
        "Lifespan recover_interrupted re-runs scans left 'accepted'/'analyzing' after a restart"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Access control",
      "items": [
        "require_api_key middleware: X-Provenyx-Key on every route except /health and OAuth redirects; GitHub Bearer accepted on /api/scans",
        "Scan rows carry owner_id (pseudonymous GitHub subject); reads use get_owned / list_recent",
        "GitHub token lives only in an AES-256-GCM sealed HTTP-only cookie; never stored server-side",
        "Sliding-window submission rate limit per client address (in-process, per worker); body capped at 10 MiB while streaming"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Release verification",
      "items": [
        "release_id = keccak256('name@version'); manifest_hash = keccak256(canonical JSON with dist.integrity)",
        "Backend only reads the chain (eth_chainId + eth_call recordOf); anchoring is an owner-only Hardhat script",
        "Results: match / mismatch / no_record / unavailable. no_record is an evidence gap, not a risk signal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Deployment & persistence",
      "items": [
        "render.yaml: python web service, rootDir backend, uvicorn --proxy-headers, health check /health, generated API key + session secret",
        "PROVENYX_DATABASE_URL: SQLite backend/provenyx.db locally, Neon Postgres in production (postgres:// normalized to psycopg; pool_pre_ping)",
        "Uncommitted in the worktree: an OpenRouter simplifier (backend/app/llm/) that summarises findings after analysis; not shown as it is not at the pinned revision"
      ]
    }
  ]
}